
[TestRule/invalid-0 - 1]
Diagnostic 1: repeatedSelection (4:22 - 4:42)
Message: This repeats a decision already made by `matches`.
Help: `matches` selects values, but `render` receives the whole type and decides again. Carry the narrowed selected value through `CatalogView` into `render`, or reuse a shared selection helper. Use a type predicate only when false excludes every value of its target too.
   3 |   matches: (item) => item.kind === "stock" && item.sku === "alpha",
   4 |   render: (item) => (item.kind === "stock" ? item.sku : undefined),
     |                      ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
   5 | });
